(Kenya-China Tea Summit 2027) Tj T*
(Connecting Tea, Cultures & Opportunities) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Dates: 21-23 April 2027) Tj T*
(Location: Nairobi, Kenya) Tj T*
(Theme: Brewing Strategic Partnerships for Sustainable Tea Trade, Investment and Innovation) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(OBJECTIVES) Tj T*
(- Strengthen trade relations: Build durable commercial links between Kenyan tea producers) Tj T*
(  and Chinese buyers.) Tj T*
(- Promote investment: Open Kenya's tea value chain to Chinese capital across processing,) Tj T*
(  packaging and logistics.) Tj T*
(- Support innovation: Bring agricultural technology, processing equipment and traceability) Tj T*
(  tools to the people who will use them.) Tj T*
(- Facilitate market access: Shorten the route from a Kenyan estate to a Chinese shelf.) Tj T*
(- Foster collaboration: Put producers, policymakers, financiers and researchers in the same) Tj T*
(  rooms for three days.) Tj T*
(- Promote tea culture: Set Kenya's tea heritage alongside China's, as trade and as culture.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(REGISTRATION CATEGORIES) Tj T*
(- Delegate: Attend the forums, conference sessions and expo.) Tj T*
(- Exhibitor: Take a stand at the International Tea & Technology Expo.) Tj T*
(- Sponsor: Partner with the summit across branding and networking.) Tj T*
(- Government: Attend in an official or trade-policy capacity.) Tj T*
(- Media: Cover the summit with accreditation.) Tj T*
(- Student: Attend at student rate as a researcher or trainee.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Organised by Kenya-China Tea Summit Secretariat, Orbitline Events & Ushers Ltd.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Current information is published at https://kenya-china-tea-summit.pages.dev) Tj T*
